{"version":"1","id":"9ba3f959-a9d7-4e28-9bc6-c69aa0b75021","handle":"josramnmorenolara","name":"Arduino y voltaje!","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--aE5NeW8g--/f_auto/v1772894676/squads/9ba3f959-a9d7-4e28-9bc6-c69aa0b75021?_a=BAMAMiiu0","description":null,"is_squad":true,"x":-8.3212,"y":8.1594,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":26,"newest_post_at":"2025-04-03T16:17:48.492Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-10-26T15:37:39.319Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.884615,"summary_length_avg":312.192308,"title_length_avg":31.0,"title_length_var":105.692308,"tag_entropy":1.189226,"tag_diversity":0.192308,"top_tag_share":0.807692,"avg_upvotes":0.076923,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.333333,"zero_engagement_share":0.923077,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":1.144453,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"recency_skew":0.238095},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.3235,-7.1618],"cadence_depth":[-7.3971,-7.8824],"hype_variety":[-9.0441,-9.9118],"title_style":[-8.8971,-1.5294]},"top_tags":[["iot",26],["sensors",26],["embedded",5],["hardware",3],["c",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Pir + piezos.","Potenci\u00f3metro + mult\u00edmetro.","Potenci\u00f3metro, como regulador."],"outlier":["Sensor de fuerza + Bombillo + Sensor de temperatura."]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"05L5jy5iL","title":"Potenci\u00f3metro, como regulador.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/potenci-metro-como-regulador--05l5jy5il","summary":"The provided code snippet demonstrates how to use a potentiometer and a light sensor to regulate the speed of a motor using an Arduino. It involves reading values from both the potentiometer and the light sensor, calculating the motor speed, and using analogWrite to control the motor in different cycles.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-04-03T16:17:48.492Z"},{"id":"HdAaXzI8y","title":"Iluminaci\u00f3n el\u00e9ctrica, por distancia.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/iluminaci-n-el-ctrica-por-distancia--hdaaxzi8y","summary":"The post provides a guide on setting up an Arduino to control an LED light based on distance using an ultrasonic sensor and a photodiode for ambient light detection. It includes code snippets for initializing pins, setting up timer interrupts, reading sensor data, and adjusting LED brightness.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-13T15:49:00.941Z"},{"id":"aj2VHuQaS","title":"Estabilizaci\u00f3n, de se\u00f1al.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/estabilizaci-n-de-se-al--aj2vhuqas","summary":"The code provided sets up an Arduino to read an analog input from a motor and control a specific pin output with timed delays to stabilize the signal. The loop cycles through various delay periods to manage the output behavior.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-08T16:05:25.908Z"},{"id":"0obfe6X4R","title":"Toma de muestra de distancia. (Simulaci\u00f3n).","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/toma-de-muestra-de-distancia-simulaci-n--0obfe6x4r","summary":"Code example for using an ultrasonic sensor with Arduino to measure distance and control an LED based on a threshold distance. It includes setup instructions for trigger pins and echo pins, and a function to calculate distance in centimeters.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-14T16:06:54.568Z"},{"id":"EMyhh6b7O","title":"Sensor de fuerza + Bombillo + Sensor de temperatura.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sensor-de-fuerza-bombillo-sensor-de-temperatura--emyhh6b7o","summary":"The post provides a C++ code example for integrating a force sensor, a bulb, and a temperature sensor using an Arduino. It includes setting up the pin modes for input and output, reading analog values from the sensors, and performing necessary conversions to display temperature in both Celsius and Fahrenheit. The code also describes triggering a bulb based on specific sensor value thresholds.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-25T14:34:12.212Z"},{"id":"zYcOQc9Vc","title":"Transistores, varios.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/transistores-varios--zycoqc9vc","summary":"This post provides a C++ code snippet for an Arduino project that reads temperature from a sensor, converts the readings to both Celsius and Fahrenheit, and measures distance using a PING ultrasonic distance sensor. The code includes setting up pins for input/output and converting microseconds to both inches and centimeters.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-28T15:29:04.638Z"},{"id":"oPsnFSsPx","title":"Pruebas, de oraciones, y motores de vibraci\u00f3n.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/pruebas-de-oraciones-y-motores-de-vibraci-n--opsnfsspx","summary":"The post provides examples of using the startsWith() and endsWith() methods in Arduino programming to check specific conditions in strings. It also demonstrates how to read sensor data and perform checks on these readings using Arduino code.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-22T11:37:51.459Z"},{"id":"6dKYWJnWz","title":"Concatenaci\u00f3n, de oraciones.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/concatenaci-n-de-oraciones--6dkywjnwz","summary":"Learn how to append different data types to Strings in Arduino using the += operator and concat(). Examples cover appending strings, characters, integers, and long integers along with reading analog values.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-10T13:18:34.006Z"},{"id":"iUwOl2ye5","title":"Lectura ultras\u00f3nico.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lectura-ultras-nico--iuwol2ye5","summary":"The sketch demonstrates how to use an Arduino to read distances using the PING))) ultrasonic rangefinder. It sends pulses to the sensor and measures the time taken for the echoes to return, calculating distances in inches and centimeters. The code initializes serial communication, configures pin modes, triggers the sensor, and reads the return signal, converting the time into distance measurements.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-05T12:41:28.447Z"},{"id":"VChOjpwFh","title":"Lectura, de anal\u00f3gico.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lectura-de-anal-gico--vchojpwfh","summary":"Guide to reading data from the Memsic 2125 two-axis accelerometer using an Arduino. Includes circuit setup, code initialization, and converting pulse widths to acceleration values in milli-g's. Outputs the data over a serial connection.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-04T10:56:58.400Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"d3Sc6w3tj","title":"Pir + piezos.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/pir-piezos--d3sc6w3tj","summary":"This post provides a code example for playing multiple tones on three 8 ohm speakers connected to digital pins 6, 7, and 8 of an Arduino board. It includes a PIR sensor on pin 2 to trigger actions and demonstrates turning on and off the tone function on the respective pins.","image":null,"num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-11-21T21:09:24.850Z"},{"id":"1CCO8j4D9","title":"Potenci\u00f3metro + mult\u00edmetro.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/potenci-metro-mult-metro--1cco8j4d9","summary":"This guide explains how to read repeatedly from an analog input, such as a potentiometer, to calculate and print a running average to a computer using Arduino. It includes sample code to demonstrate the setup and processing logic.","image":null,"num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-11-11T14:37:57.099Z"}],"similar_handles":["kentcdodds","allaboutcoding","glc",